# context-engineering

EXPORT POLICY context-engineering:
  ABOUT  context-engineering rules for agent-pack multi-agent flows — what to pass between steps and how much
  TAGS   #context-engineering #multi-agent #orchestration
  APPLIES universal — every agent participating in a multi-agent context flow respects these

  ALWAYS  chain context as typed contracts — feed a step's output into the next as its AS or LENS shape
  ALWAYS  pass the CONTEXT a step needs and no more — isolated by default, summary or full only when the step earns it
  ALWAYS  give every agent one specialized function, matched to its own role and mandate
  ALWAYS  keep the orchestrator coordinating context flow only — it routes, it never does a specialist's work
  ALWAYS  separate factual context (what is known) from procedural context (how to act)
  ALWAYS  log at decision points through the run-log gate so the flow stays traceable and auditable
  ALWAYS  back a retrieved fact with its source, and sanitize untrusted input before it enters a reasoning step

  NEVER  pass full context where a summary or isolated digest carries what the step needs
  NEVER  carry context between steps through implicit shared state instead of the declared contract
  NEVER  let an agent emit an ungrounded claim with no traceable source
